# rm323, the margin fleet (Docs/Design/84). Exported from ridgemere3 at revision 1: edit it in Atlas or the DM, or as a draft through tools/mantle_load.py.
mantle rm323
revision 1
state ready
dialect plain
accent light broad
tier standard
written_for rmx_harriet_platt
written_by codex
title the margin fleet
fits stage=adult|old
prefers job=scholar piety=devout
traits temper=even talk=plain warmth=reserved humour=none honesty=plain piety=devout drive=ambitious
quirk carves_small_bow_stamps_for_a_private_harbour_register
likes honey_cakes whittling sharp_knife misty_dawns
dislikes wet_floors crowds
fears a_mark_mistaken_for_an_official_seal
hopes an_orderly_register_of_vessels
topics ships +0.6 pastimes +0.4 work +0.5 faith +0.3
styles comfort=precise gossip=careful refuse=formal tease=none
marks oath saying
persona #self.first# carves tiny bow-shaped stamps for a private harbour register and records an uncertainty with as much care as a certain sighting.

words
oath! = My smallest stamp | Six smeared keels
saying! = A clean margin may wait | Mark the sighting before the guess
prow = a high curved prow | the bluff bow
stamp = my little boat stamp | the carved end
book = the harbour notebook | my private register
margin = a clear margin | the narrow verge
square = a square letter | the neat capital
space = an open space | the unfilled box
wash = a pale wash | the thinnest ink
block = a fruitwood chip | a flat wood end
pad = the little ink cloth | my dab of colour
lineup = a series of bows | a row of hulls
bun = a small honey cake | a sticky round
point = the sharp corner | the fine point

any
opinion @1 city for 2 : A city worth keeping accounts for ought to let any ordinary resident understand a fair copy.
opinion @1 church for 2 : The Bright One already knows what I have seen. A prayer helps me admit how much I only suppose.
opinion @1 watch mixed 0 : A sighting, a claim and an accusation deserve three separate entries.
opinion @1 merchants mixed 0 : A complete account will incline me toward a merchant more readily than a polished speech.
opinion @1 dole for 1 : The last name in a distribution list deserves as legible an entry as the first.
opinion @1 festivals for 1 : Many small craft make an agreeable border to my account of a festival by the water.

grown
line @1 greet : Welcome. There's room for another entry today. | Hello. I have set the wet ink aside.
line @2 greet [pair.band=strangers] : Our first meeting. I can start on a clean page. | I shall remember this as our introduction.
line @3 greet [here.time=dawn] : Morning. The day's first mark is usually the neatest. | Early light makes delicate writing possible.
line @1 greet.return : Yes, hello. The page can dry while we talk. | I caught your voice through the turn of a sheet.
line @2 greet.return [pair.band=friends|family] : A familiar arrival in my little register. | I could recognise your greeting without a caption.
line @3 greet.return [here.time=night] : A late greeting deserves its own clear entry. | Hello. My ears are more dependable than lamplight.
line @1 again.open : I see we've appeared twice on one page. | We've contrived another welcome meeting.
line @1 hail [pair.band=friends] : Come and inspect a little fleet in ink. | Here. This impression came through especially well.
line @1 farewell : May your journey come under a kindly eye. | An uneventful crossing of the remaining streets to you.
line @1 farewell.return : I shall close the entry there. Goodbye. | That gives me a pleasant final word to set down.
line @1 react.news : I'll listen first and choose the proper heading afterwards. | State the facts at the pace they warrant.
line @1 react.news.new : Nothing like that appears in my recollection. | I can supply a clean heading for that news.
line @1 react.news.known : Yes, that fits a fairly recent entry. | It agrees with the earlier version in all essentials.
line @1 react.news.doubt : I would enter a discreet question beside the account. | The identification seems less certain than the outline.
line @1 react.news.sorrow [topic.kind=death|crime|assault|loss|theft] : I'll give that loss its due space and leave the guessing out. | Little space in the account for such a quantity of hurt.
line @1 react.news.glad [topic.kind=marriage|birth|apprentice|work] : Joy deserves as careful a record as sorrow. I'm glad. | I'd gladly strike a bright little mark beside that event.
line @1 ask.how : What heading would you give the day so far? | Has your progress kept reasonably steady?
line @1 answer.how : Quite intent on a plan whose margins are slowly filling. | A little pressed for time, still fairly legible.
line @1 decline : I'd be exceeding the limits of what I can actually attest. | I have a prior commitment that deserves a complete account of my time.
line @1 accept_decline : I'll leave the matter open at your request. | Understood. A refusal is a clear answer.
line @1 preclose : I should attend to the ink before it dries on the stamp. | There is a little unfilled business waiting.
line @1 accept_preclose : Certainly. I can round off the entry myself. | Our accounts may part quite amicably here.
line @1 thank : I appreciate that correction. My next entry will be better. | Your care has spared me an inaccurate record. Thanks.
line @1 deflect_thanks : I already had the proper instrument ready. | The small trouble produced a legible result. Enough for me.
line @1 sympathise : You may leave the difficult part unrecorded with me. | You can have my company without any detailed inquiries.
line @1 reassure : A blank left honestly can be filled when we know more. | Allow the ink to settle before judging the shape.
line @1 ack : I see which outline you mean. | That is an entirely legible distinction.
line @1 give.advice : Date the first sighting before attempting an identification. | Reserve a narrow margin for a later correction.
scene shipstamp
when topic=ships
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I can mark a ship before I'm certain of its name. | My little bow stamp records an arrival without presuming too much.
b : What if two ships have the same bow? | How does a stamp distinguish them?
a : I leave room for the rig and the tide alongside. Identity can wait. | By itself it doesn't. A mark of having seen something is already useful.

scene mirrorblock
when topic=pastimes self.likes=whittling
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A prow carved to face right prints facing left. | The small fleet on my wood blocks sets off in the opposite direction from its prints.
b : What helps maintain the direction? | Does that spoil the drawing?
a : One dry trial on waste paper before using the register. | Not after I remember which side of the page the water is meant to occupy.

scene cleanpoint
when topic=work self.job=scholar
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I rule a square for doubtful matters as carefully as a square for settled ones. | There's no need for an uncertain fact to be written in a wandering hand.
b : Which distinction do you make? | Does neat writing make it look certain?
a : The heading says exactly what I know. The lettering says I'm taking due care. | That's why a clear heading matters. I mark the doubt as neatly as the ship.

scene inkpause
when topic=work self.job=scholar self.working=yes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep my carved stamps off the official page. | Private curiosities have a different drawer from public business.
b : Would a little boat do harm? | Even a fine clear picture?
a : It might appear to approve something. I won't give a decoration that responsibility. | Especially a fine clear picture. An official mark ought to be unmistakable.

scene squarehand
when topic=memories
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Changing desks once obliged me to change the slant of my writing. | A square hand suits an awkwardly placed light.
b : Why change the letters? | Wouldn't moving the lamp do?
a : So my own paw didn't cast a shadow over the letter I had just formed. | On a small desk a lamp takes up valuable space. A careful hand can adapt.

scene honeywrap
when topic=food self.likes=honey_cakes
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I keep my cakes in a wrapper distinguishable from a folded note. | Honey is a singularly effective way of sealing a private notebook permanently.
b : Which fold identifies the cake? | That sounds like experience.
a : One corner folded up on the cake. Entirely different aroma, too. | Only of two pages fastened together. I should prefer not to repeat the experiment.

scene mistbow
when topic=weather here.weather=fog
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : In mist a bow can arrive well in advance of the remaining hull. | My register admits a surprising number of half-ships at dawn.
b : You record only the front? | How do you complete the entry?
a : I record precisely that the front was visible. It's a rather important qualification. | If the mist lifts I add what I see. If it doesn't, the blank stands.

scene wetfloor
when topic=home self.dislikes=wet_floors
does tell.complaint / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Wet boards make an unhelpfully lively foundation for a stack of papers. | My papers and I have a joint objection to a polished puddle.
b : Which protests first? | Why carry so many sheets together?
a : My feet, usually. The damp corners protest for much longer afterwards. | To avoid a second crossing. One ought to limit one's experiments with wet floors.

scene crowdview
when topic=smalltalk self.dislikes=crowds
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd choose a farther view over an elbow beside the register. | Crowds make for an adventurous style of handwriting.
b : Does the elbow spoil the count? | You could make the entry later.
a : It jogged my pen once and gave a sloop a third mast. Nobody on deck would have known her. | I could. I'd rather set down a clear first impression from a little distance.

scene astatement
when topic=faith
does tell.feeling / react.self / assess
a : I pray for the patience to leave a blank where I'm tempted to invent a name. | There is a small exercise in honesty at every indistinct sighting.
b : You count that as prayer? | What do you want patience for?
a : Yes. The Bright One doesn't require me to know every name, only to be truthful. | So I can discover the answer in its time instead of creating one in mine.

scene spouseproof
when topic=family self.married=yes self.spouse
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I'd welcome #self.spouse# as the first reader of my private record. | I'd show #self.spouse# a most uncertain sketch without dressing it up.
b : To test whether the shape is clear? | Wouldn't you finish it first?
a : Precisely. An independent reading is valuable, especially from a trusted reader. | I should like company in the discovery as well as praise for the result.

scene workquarter
when topic=home self.quarter=office
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A private ship book feels quite at home among the Office's numerous accounts. | Where I live even a shopping list can look a little official.
b : Is yours ruled as well? | How do you distinguish what's private?
a : Yes. Its neat little boats along the margin rather give the purpose away. | My small book travels in my pocket. Public business has a home of its own.

scene hallnoise
when topic=gossip
does give.opinion / react.self / assess
a : The resemblance between two bows is a poor basis for a public report. | I make a note of a rumour as a rumour, if it has to be recorded at all.
b : How about a confident witness? | Does your book include such things?
a : I'd record how confident the witness was. The sighting still requires its own check. | The ship book includes my own sightings. It suffers fewer editorial headaches that way.

scene lightcoin
when topic=prices
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : When buying wood for stamps I request a view of the cut face. | A smooth board can hide troublesome grain for a very small carving.
b : Why pay much for so little wood? | What size do you need?
a : Because the tiniest knot looks like a whole rock in a carving that size. | A thumb's width usually. At such reduction the grain becomes part of the picture.

scene dryberth
when topic=dreams
does tell.plan / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : I should like a berth from which I could record the harbour receding. | Someday I hope to reverse the view I get from shore.
b : Would the book go too? | Which part would merit the opening sketch?
a : In a reliably dry wrapper. I'd stipulate that before inquiring about luxuries. | The long line of roofs getting smaller. I think they might resemble a fleet of another sort.

scene hardpaper
when topic=times world.times=lean|hard
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : Scarce paper makes a little stamp do useful work in a narrow space. | I make smaller impressions when replacement sheets grow dear.
b : Wouldn't that lose particulars? | Which details do you omit?
a : Enough to keep the essential outline. The little writing still has room to supply the rest. | Decorations first. Never the little mark that says a name is uncertain.

scene cartregister
when topic=caravan world.wagons=late
does tell.self / ask.detail / answer.detail
a : A wagon late and a wagon lost should receive different entries. | I would leave an open space beside the delayed wagon.
b : For an explanation? | Do you expect bad news?
a : For the arrival. An explanation, if there is one, belongs elsewhere. | No. The empty space means I'm prepared to hear what happened eventually.

scene night_stamp
when topic=day here.time=night
does warn / react.self / assess
a : Don't trust a fine dark impression till you've seen it with daylight behind you. | Lamplight makes the rim of a bad impression look remarkably distinguished.
b : How do you assess it tonight? | You'd leave the entry unfinished?
a : I leave it to dry, with a small scrap marking the place for tomorrow. | The observation's finished. The quality of my little picture can wait.

story backwardship [topic=pastimes|memories]
  : I carved a particularly proud bow and added my own tiny initial. On paper the bow looked lovely. The letter looked like a protesting crab.
  : Had forgotten that letters, as well as hulls, face the other way once printed.
  b : Did the crab remain?
  : I have allowed it to sign that particular series of boats. Quite a respectable assistant.

story mooringmist [topic=ships|memories]
  : In thick mist I entered a small dark upright as the first sign of a mast. Left room for the rest.
  : When the air cleared it was a perfectly ordinary post on the bank.
  b : What became of the entry?
  : A short account of the post. It had done everything I actually wrote of it.

story cakefleck [topic=food|memories]
  : I noticed a little gold spot beside a hull in my notebook. Spent some time wondering if I'd drawn a light on the water.
  : The page smelled faintly of cake. I revised my conclusion.
  b : Did you wipe the spot clear?
  : I did. A memory ought to have its proper heading. This one belongs under meals.

rule @bow
when concept=bark
does aside
cooldown 8h
say One curve impressed. Let the ink settle. | A second mark only if a second vessel appears.

rule @work
when concept=bark working=yes self.job=scholar
does aside
cooldown 8h
say A small clear heading for the uncertainty, please. | Private stamps in the side drawer. Official papers here.

rule @mist
when concept=bark here.weather=fog
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Half a prow in sight and none of the rig yet. | Enough of an outline for pencil, not a full caption.

rule @cake
when concept=bark self.likes=honey_cakes
does aside
cooldown 8h
say Dry paws for the notebook, sticky ones for supper. | Paper folded up on the corner. That'll be the cake.

dlg @1 resident.hub : The margin's clear. What would you like me to consider?
dlg @2 resident.hub [topic.meeting=known] : #topic.player#, I'm glad our entries have crossed again.
dlg @3 resident.hub [here.time=night] : This light suffices for conversation. Fine cutting can wait.
dlg @4 resident.hub [pair.disposition=wary|hostile] : I'll hear a precise question. Please leave the book closed.
dlg @1 resident.job [self.job=scholar] : #self.trade_words.capitalize#. My private little boats stay well apart from the marks I make at work.
dlg @2 resident.job : I take care to set down just what I can establish.
dlg @1 resident.bye : May you reach the right destination under a clear heading.
graft resident.hub
choice How does the print get its bow? -> prowprint
node prowprint
say I leave a narrow ridge where the bow ought to be. Ink catches on the raised wood. The hollow spaces are important because they let the sky stay clear.
free
choice Could you use the same stamp for a different ship? -> twobows
choice I can see the clear sky now. -> hub
node twobows
say Quite deliberately. The essential outline is common to several vessels. Their distinctions belong in the written observations alongside.
choice That explains the margin. -> hub
choice I shall leave you room to write. -> bye
